                    },
                    "message": "Should we also document the PCIe Switch interface here?"
                },
                {
                    "file": "yaml/xyz/openbmc_project/Metric/Value.interface.yaml",
                    "line": 57,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Harshit Aghera",
                        "email": "haghera@nvidia.com",
                        "username": "harshit-aghera"
                    },
                    "message": "Correction - It should be Port Interface since these are Port metrics."
                },
                {
                    "file": "yaml/xyz/openbmc_project/Metric/Value.interface.yaml",
                    "line": 57,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Deepak Kodihalli",
                        "email": "deepak.kodihalli.83@gmail.com",
                        "username": "dkodihal"
                    },
                    "message": "I don't think so. Instead, we should add Inventory.Item to the inventory object that implements Port. Inventory associations are collectively documented in Inventory.Item."
                },
                {
                    "file": "yaml/xyz/openbmc_project/Metric/Value.interface.yaml",
                    "line": 137,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Gunnar Mills",
                        "email": "gunnar@gmills.xyz",
                        "username": "gtmills"
                    },
                    "message": "Some more explaining what a reply is, might be helpful. \" A replay is a retransmission of a TLP and occurs because the ACK timer is expired, which means that the receiver did not send the ACK or this device did not properly decode the ACK.\""
                },
                {
                    "file": "yaml/xyz/openbmc_project/Metric/Value.interface.yaml",
                    "line": 137,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Deepak Kodihalli",
                        "email": "deepak.kodihalli.83@gmail.com",
                        "username": "dkodihal"
                    },
                    "message": "Acknowledged"
                },
                {
                    "file": "yaml/xyz/openbmc_project/Metric/Value.interface.yaml",
                    "line": 141,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Gunnar Mills",
                        "email": "gunnar@gmills.xyz",
                        "username": "gtmills"
                    },
                    "message": "Might be good to expand on what this is. From https://redfish.dmtf.org/schemas/v1/PCIeDevice.v1_20_0.json#/definitions/PCIeErrors \n\nA replay rollover occurs when consecutive replays failed to resolve the errors on the link, which means that this device forced the link into the recovery state."
                },
