            "comments": [
                {
                    "file": "/PATCHSET_LEVEL",
                    "line": 0,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Deepak Kodihalli",
                        "email": "deepak.kodihalli.83@gmail.com",
                        "username": "dkodihal"
                    },
                    "message": "@gunnar@gmills.xyz I've addressed your review comments. Can you please re-review? The child commit as well please?\n\n@patrick@stwcx.xyz @paligill@gmail.com can I get feedback on this and the child commit please?"
                },
                {
                    "file": "yaml/xyz/openbmc_project/Metric/Value.interface.yaml",
                    "line": 121,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Patrick Williams",
                        "email": "patrick@stwcx.xyz",
                        "username": "williamspatrick"
                    },
                    "message": "pcie wouldn't be part of the URI here.\n\nYou might need a separate namespace for PCIe?  Or ... how are these attached to a device?\n\nWe typically have something like `.../metric/bmc/cpu/total`.  So the BMC namespace + a path segment for the metric.\n\n`correctable_error_count` or `memory/correctable_error_count` might make sense here and then add some kind of PCIe namespace.  But... I suspect you want these associated with a particular device?  So we need to define how the translation from device to path works."
                },
                {
                    "file": "yaml/xyz/openbmc_project/Metric/Value.interface.yaml",
                    "line": 121,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Deepak Kodihalli",
                        "email": "deepak.kodihalli.83@gmail.com",
                        "username": "dkodihal"
                    },
                    "message": "Separated out PCIe vs generic metrics.\n\nAdded namespace for PCIe."
                },
                {
                    "file": "yaml/xyz/openbmc_project/Metric/Value.interface.yaml",
                    "line": 121,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Deepak Kodihalli",
                        "email": "deepak.kodihalli.83@gmail.com",
                        "username": "dkodihal"
                    },
                    "message": "Actually only a single namespace is allowed (which makes sense, say to avoid conflicts in namespaces). For things like total memory vs total cpu, I see both cpu/total and memory/total defined - that is, we didn't define cpu and memory as namespaces and total as the metric. I've followed the same for PCIe metrics, and once could add a subset of these with memory/<metric> when there's a need."
                },
                {
                    "file": "yaml/xyz/openbmc_project/Metric/Value.interface.yaml",
                    "line": 134,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Patrick Williams",
                        "email": "patrick@stwcx.xyz",
                        "username": "williamspatrick"
                    },
                    "message": "This one does sound PCIe-specific because it is talking about a particular training procedure that is unique to PCIe.  So maybe PCIe is still appropriate on this one.  We're still needing to define how we map a particular PCIe device to a metric path."
                },
                {
                    "file": "yaml/xyz/openbmc_project/Metric/Value.interface.yaml",
                    "line": 134,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Deepak Kodihalli",
                        "email": "deepak.kodihalli.83@gmail.com",
                        "username": "dkodihal"
                    },
                    "message": "Will add a device path for the relevant device here (which is actually a port)."
                },
                {
                    "file": "yaml/xyz/openbmc_project/Metric/Value.interface.yaml",
                    "line": 134,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Deepak Kodihalli",
                        "email": "deepak.kodihalli.83@gmail.com",
                        "username": "dkodihal"
                    },
                    "message": "Acknowledged"
                }
            ],
